{
 "openingTheDialogAndPlanning": [
  [
   "modal",
   "Change storage class · data",
   "<p class=\"ui-lead\">Copy this volume to another storage class, keeping its name. Apps and VMs using it stop during the move, and the original data is kept afterwards.</p><div class=\"ui-fields\"><div class=\"ui-field\">\n    <label for=\"field-c1\">From</label><input id=\"field-c1\" value=\"old\" disabled></div><div class=\"ui-field\">\n    <label for=\"rc_to\">To</label><select id=\"rc_to\" onchange=\"volumeReclassPlan(\"lab\",\"data\")\"><option value=\"new-class\" selected>new-class</option><option value=\"other\" >other</option></select></div></div><div id=\"rc_plan\"></div><label class=\"ui-ack\">\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"rc_ack\" onchange=\"volumeReclassReady()\"><span>Copy it despite the downtime and warnings</span></label><div class=\"ui-actions\" >\n      <div class=\"ui-actions-start\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"closeModal()\" data-dialog-dismiss=\"true\">Cancel</button></div><div class=\"ui-actions-end\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn pri\" id=\"rc_go\" onclick=\"volumeReclassStart(\"lab\",\"data\")\" disabled >Move volume</button></div></div>",
   false,
   "operation-review"
  ],
  [
   "api",
   "/api/volumes/reclass/plan",
   {
    "namespace": "lab",
    "claim": "data",
    "target": "new-class"
   }
  ],
  [
   "applyRole"
  ],
  [
   "state",
   "planned",
   "<div class=\"ui-callout info\" role=\"note\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-info\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><b>This can move with nothing stopped</b><div class=\"ui-callout-body\"><p>new-class differs from old only in which disks hold the copies (nvme). Its copies can move there while it stays in use, and the volume keeps the class name old.</p>\n     <div class=\"row\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn pri\" onclick=\"volumeCopyMove(window.__reclassVolume,{\"disk_tags\":[\"nvme\"],\"node_tags\":[]})\" data-need=\"operator\">Move copies instead</button></div></div></div>\n    </div><div class=\"ui-callout warn\" role=\"alert\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-alert\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><div class=\"ui-notice-line ui-notice-whole\"><b class=\"ui-notice-head\">Before moving</b><span class=\"ui-notice-first ui-issue-short\">Capacity unknown</span></div></div>\n    </div><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Affected apps and VMs</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"ui-table-wrap\"><table class=\"ui-table stack\"><thead><tr><th class=\"\">App or VM</th><th class=\"\">Effect</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody><tr><td class=\"\" data-label=\"App or VM\">&lt;app> · Deployment</td><td class=\"\" data-label=\"Effect\">stopped, then started again</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Storage needed</h4></header>\n    <dl class=\"ui-facts\"><div><dt>New volume</dt><dd>20 GiB</dd></div><div><dt>Replica allocation</dt><dd>40 GiB · 2 copies</dd></div><div><dt>Estimated destination room</dt><dd>Unknown</dd></div></dl></section><details class=\"ui-more\" data-disclosure=\"What is checked\">\n    <summary>What is checked</summary><div class=\"ui-more-body\">The volume, its disk, the destination class and the affected apps and VMs are checked again before starting. Missing information stops the move. This does not reserve storage or capacity, and recovery and host failure checks are separate. Both copies use space until the original is removed.</div></details>",
   true,
   false,
   false
  ]
 ],
